<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    XFB is reached over the local network at a plain http:// address, so
    cleartext has to be permitted.

    It would be better to permit it only for private address ranges, but the
    network security config has no way to express that: <domain> matches
    hostnames only, and CIDR notation in it silently matches nothing at all.
    The station's address is whatever the operator's router handed out, so
    there is no static host list to enumerate either.

    This is the weakest point in the sync design and it is deliberate for now —
    tokens and audio cross the LAN unencrypted. Pinning a self-signed
    certificate at pairing time is the eventual fix, and would let this go back
    to denying cleartext outright.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
